<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><link rel="icon" href="data:,"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="color-scheme" content="dark"><title>PROMETHEUS / KITTY Mission Studio</title><style>__STYLE__</style></head>
<body><div id="app"><header class="topbar"><a class="brand" href="#" aria-label="Prometheus home"><span class="brand-mark">P<span>•</span></span><div>PROMETHEUS<small>KITTY CORP / MISSION STUDIO</small></div></a><div class="status-chip"><i></i> SOFTWARE PROTOTYPE</div><div class="top-actions"><span id="perf">INITIALIZING GPU</span><select id="quality" aria-label="Graphics quality"><option value="auto" selected>Auto GPU</option><option value="1">Performance</option><option value="1.5">Balanced</option><option value="2">High GPU</option></select><button id="help-open" class="icon-button" title="Guide and evidence">?</button></div></header>
<nav class="modebar" aria-label="Workspace"><button data-mode="hero" class="active">01 <span>Showcase</span></button><button data-mode="mission">02 <span>Mission lab</span></button><button data-mode="wiring">03 <span>Engineering</span></button><button data-mode="architecture">04 <span>Laptop brain</span></button><button data-mode="future">05 <span>Future concept</span></button></nav>
<main><section class="viewport-shell" id="stage"><img id="fallback" src="__FALLBACK__" alt="Saved KITTY chassis preview"><canvas id="viewport" aria-label="Interactive 3D robot and test world"></canvas><div class="viewport-title"><span id="eyebrow">VISION-BASED ASSISTANT / VIRTUAL PROTOTYPE</span><h1 id="scene-title">Small robot.<br><em>Connected mind.</em></h1><p id="scene-copy">Phone senses. Laptop thinks. KITTY responds.</p></div><div class="viewport-badges"><span id="view-label">V7.1 BODY + PLANNED SENSOR ADDITIONS</span><span id="scope-label">SIMULATION</span></div><div class="camera-tools"><button data-camera="hero" title="Hero view">Hero</button><button data-camera="orbit" title="Orbit controls">Orbit</button><button data-camera="top" title="Overhead view">Top</button><button data-camera="follow" title="Follow robot">Follow</button><button data-camera="eye" title="Robot eye view">Robot eye</button><button id="snapshot">PNG</button></div><div id="graphics-error" hidden><strong>Graphics is unavailable</strong><p id="graphics-message">The saved model remains visible. Enable graphics acceleration and retry.</p><button id="retry-gpu">Retry graphics</button></div><div id="labels"></div><div class="telemetry-strip"><div><span>CONTROLLER</span><strong id="state">IDLE</strong></div><div><span>FRONT / REAR</span><strong id="ranges">— / —</strong></div><div><span>RADAR SERVO</span><strong id="servo-angle">0°</strong></div><div><span>VIRTUAL SPEED</span><strong id="speed">0.00 m/s</strong></div></div><div id="toast" role="status"></div></section>
<aside class="console"><section class="panel" id="mission-panel"><div class="panel-heading"><span class="kicker">MISSION CONTROL</span><span class="mini-status" id="circuit-status">MODEL READY</span></div><h2 id="mission-heading">Give the idea a destination.</h2><p class="muted" id="reason">Choose a mission or play the guided demonstration.</p><div class="button-row"><button id="navigate" class="primary">Go to marker <span>↗</span></button><button id="home">Return home</button></div><div class="button-row"><button id="follow-marker">Track camera marker</button><button id="add-obstacle">+ Obstacle</button></div><div class="mode-row"><label><input type="checkbox" id="show-sensors" checked> Sensor cones</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="show-path" checked> Path</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="xray"> X-ray</label></div><div id="manual" class="manual"><button data-drive="forward" aria-label="Drive forward">↑</button><div><button data-drive="left" aria-label="Turn left">←</button><button data-drive="back" aria-label="Drive backward">↓</button><button data-drive="right" aria-label="Turn right">→</button></div><small>Hold to drive · WASD · release stops</small></div><div class="stop-row"><button id="estop" class="danger">■ LATCH STOP</button><button id="reset">Reset / disarm</button></div></section>
<section class="panel camera-panel"><div class="panel-heading"><span class="kicker" id="camera-heading">PHONE CAMERA → LAPTOP</span><span class="mini-status" id="camera-source">SYNTHETIC RGB</span></div><canvas id="camera-feed" width="320" height="180" aria-label="Simulated robot-eye camera with colour-marker detector"></canvas><div class="camera-caption"><span id="vision-status">Colour-marker tracker initializing</span><span id="vision-age">—</span></div></section>
<section class="panel map-panel"><div class="panel-heading"><span class="kicker">SENSOR FUSION / LOCAL MAP</span><span id="map-mode" class="mini-status">OCCUPANCY + A*</span></div><canvas id="map" width="440" height="290" aria-label="Interactive occupancy map; click to set a virtual goal"></canvas><div class="map-legend"><span><i class="mint"></i> Range hit</span><span><i class="purple"></i> A* path</span><span><i class="yellow"></i> Servo scan</span></div><small class="muted">Click a free map location to request a route. Unknown cells remain provisional.</small></section>
<section class="panel brain-panel"><div class="panel-heading"><span class="kicker">KITTY / LAPTOP BRAIN</span><button id="prompt-open" class="text-button">System prompt ↗</button></div><div class="brain-identity"><canvas id="face" width="300" height="150" aria-label="Animated KITTY face"></canvas><div><b id="brain-mode">OFFLINE DEMO RULES</b><small>Conversation requests intent.<br>The local guard owns motion.</small></div></div><div id="chat-log" role="log" aria-live="polite"><p class="reply">Hi, I’m KITTY. Let’s make a sensible entrance.</p></div><form id="chat-form"><input id="chat-input" maxlength="1000" placeholder="Ask: what do you see?" aria-label="Message KITTY"><button type="submit" id="send-chat" aria-label="Send message">↗</button><button type="button" id="voice-input" aria-label="Use browser microphone">Mic</button></form><div class="mode-row"><label><input id="audio" type="checkbox"> Buzzer audio</label><label><input id="narration" type="checkbox"> English narration</label></div></section>
<section class="panel" id="fault-panel"><div class="panel-heading"><span class="kicker">FAULT LAB</span><button id="faults-clear" class="text-button">Clear inputs</button></div><div class="fault-grid"><label><input type="checkbox" data-fault="front"> Front no-echo</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-fault="rear"> Rear missing</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-fault="radar"> Radar missing</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-fault="link"> Link lost</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-fault="camera"> Camera stale</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="cutoff-open"> Motor cutoff open</label></div><p class="muted">Restoring an input never resumes a latched mission. Reset, then request a new mission.</p></section>
<section class="panel" id="wiring-panel" hidden><div class="panel-heading"><span class="kicker">VIRTUAL WIRING WORKBENCH</span><span class="mini-status">NOMINAL MODEL</span></div><p class="muted">Simulation preset, not released physical wiring. No motor-current, transient or component-fit validation.</p><label class="field">From endpoint<select id="wire-a"></select></label><label class="field">To endpoint<select id="wire-b"></select></label><div class="button-row"><button id="wire-add">Connect endpoints</button><button id="wire-restore">Restore circuit</button></div><label class="field">Inspect / remove<select id="wire-select"></select></label><div class="button-row"><button id="wire-remove">Remove wire</button><button id="wire-empty">Clear all wires</button></div><div id="circuit-problems"></div><div class="probe-row"><select id="probe-a" aria-label="Red nominal probe"></select><select id="probe-b" aria-label="Black nominal probe"></select><strong id="probe-value">— V</strong></div><small class="muted">Ideal DC rails / signal HIGH levels. Floating nodes are N/A. Not a measured multimeter reading.</small><div class="button-row"><button id="explode">Explode assembly</button><button id="wire-view">Hide wires</button></div><div id="component-list"></div></section>
<section class="panel" id="architecture-panel" hidden><div class="panel-heading"><span class="kicker">THE SIGNAL JOURNEY</span><span class="mini-status">SIMULATED PIPELINE</span></div><ol class="pipeline"><li><b>Phone camera + microphone</b><small>RGB view and user intent. Animated screen stays on the phone.</small></li><li><b>Laptop perception + map</b><small>Pixel colour-marker tracker; range-hit occupancy and A* route.</small></li><li><b>Prompted assistant</b><small>Offline rules by default. Optional configured local model produces conversation and bounded intent.</small></li><li><b>Deterministic controller</b><small>Obstacle, frame age, link, stop latch and command limits.</small></li><li><b>ESP32 → driver → wheels</b><small>Illustrated transport only. No real device connection exists.</small></li><li><b>Phone face + external speaker</b><small>Shared expression, LED and buzzer state. Optional browser narration.</small></li></ol></section>
<section class="panel" id="future-panel" hidden><div class="panel-heading"><span class="kicker">FUTURE / PROJECT AEROKITTY</span><span class="concept-tag">CONCEPT ANIMATION</span></div><h2>One silhouette.<br>Two modes.</h2><p class="muted">Four wheels on the ground. Four folding wheel/rotor pods in the air. Explore the transformation study.</p><div class="button-row"><button id="future-drive">Four-wheel drive</button><button id="future-transform">Transform + fly</button></div><label class="field">Concept timeline<input type="range" id="future-seek" min="0" max="25" step="0.1" value="0"></label><div class="future-spec"><div><b id="future-alt">0.00 m</b><small>ANIMATED ALTITUDE</small></div><div><b id="future-fold">0%</b><small>POD DEPLOYMENT</small></div></div><p class="concept-note">This is a design animation. Flight needs a new airframe, verified mass/thrust, brushless motors + ESCs, suitable power, an autopilot and physical validation. BO motors/TB6612 are not a drone flight system.</p></section>
<section class="panel log-panel"><div class="panel-heading"><span class="kicker">DECISION TRACE</span><button id="export-events" class="text-button">Export ↗</button></div><div id="event-log" role="log"></div></section></aside></main>
<footer class="transport"><button id="demo-play" class="play-button">▶ Play guided demo</button><div class="timeline"><div class="timeline-label"><span id="chapter-name">Meet KITTY</span><span id="demo-time">00:00 / 02:12</span></div><input id="demo-seek" type="range" min="0" max="132" step="0.1" value="0" aria-label="Guided demo timeline"></div><button id="record" class="record-button"><i></i> Record video</button><button id="project-save">Save project</button><button id="project-open">Open project</button><input id="project-file" type="file" accept="application/json" hidden></footer><div id="caption" class="caption"><span>SOFTWARE PROTOTYPE</span><p>Phone senses. Laptop thinks. KITTY responds.</p></div></div>
<dialog id="help"><button class="dialog-close" data-close="help">×</button><span class="kicker">START HERE</span><h2>Your prototype, ready to present.</h2><p>Use current desktop Chrome or Edge with graphics acceleration enabled. This single HTML works offline. GPU renders 3D; CPU runs sensing/planning; RAM holds the embedded model. Actual performance depends on your machine.</p><ol><li>Press <b>Play guided demo</b> for the English presentation.</li><li>In Mission lab, choose a goal, add obstacles or try the fault toggles. Space latches STOP.</li><li>Engineering exposes the interior, simulated wires and nominal voltage checks. Use Orbit to inspect.</li><li>Future concept shows the separate four-wheel folding/flight animation.</li><li>Record video downloads a WebM with the 3D view, map, camera, state and visible prototype/concept labels. Use your screen recorder if MediaRecorder is unavailable. Browser narration is not mixed into this WebM.</li></ol><p>Ranges, camera scene and motion are simulated. The marker tracker processes rendered pixels; it is not general object recognition. This is not SPICE, a firmware emulator, real hardware control or aerodynamic simulation. The third ultrasonic and servo mount are planned additions. Existing physical wiring and print files are unchanged.</p><p>Optional local AI: run the supplied loopback Python server with an already installed Ollama model. No model weights or accounts are bundled. The standalone file uses clearly labelled offline rules.</p><button data-close="help" class="primary">Open the studio</button></dialog>
<dialog id="prompt-dialog"><button class="dialog-close" data-close="prompt-dialog">×</button><span class="kicker">LAPTOP PERSONALITY / INTENT CONTRACT</span><h2>The prompt behind KITTY.</h2><textarea id="system-prompt" spellcheck="false" aria-label="Editable assistant system prompt">__PROMPT__</textarea><p>Local edits are used for optional model requests. The program still validates the returned intent; model output cannot clear a stop latch or reach physical hardware.</p><div class="button-row"><button id="prompt-save" class="primary">Apply prompt</button><button id="prompt-download">Download prompt</button></div><p id="model-info">Open the bundled local server to use an explicitly configured Ollama model. Standalone HTML uses offline demo rules.</p></dialog>
<canvas id="recording-canvas" width="1920" height="1080" hidden></canvas>
<script id="model-data" type="application/json">__MODEL__</script><script>__THREE__</script><script>__ORBIT__</script><script>__CORE__</script><script>__APP__</script></body></html>
